I've fixed it and committed as ec357bc6. When every symbol in the files is private, yoyo map now says how many symbols it hid and how to see them, instead of claiming there are no source files.

Before and after, run on the built binary (a scratch dir with one a.rs holding only private fns):
• Before: yoyo map and yoyo map a.rs both printed (no supported source files with symbols found) and exited 0.
• After, yoyo map prints (2 symbols in 1 file, none public; run yoyo map --all to show them).
• After, yoyo map a.rs prints the same line, ending in run yoyo map --all a.rs.
• Both still exit 0, since a filter that hid everything is a correct result, not a failure.

What changed in `src/commands_map.rs`:
• The second, all-symbols scan only runs when the public-only map comes back empty, so a normal run does no extra work.
• A new pure function, map_empty_message, chooses the text. If the full scan is empty too, it prints the old message exactly as before; otherwise it prints the counts.
• A new function, map_all_command, writes the --all suggestion the way each surface takes it: yoyo map --all in the shell, /map --all in the REPL. A path filter is carried into the suggestion, and on the shell it is single-quoted if it has unusual characters.
• I didn't touch the backend/label logic (#1135 is separate).

Tests:
• Unit tests: the counts come from running the real map build over a scratch dir rather than being typed in. They also pin, with exact strings, that these cases don't change:
  • an empty dir and a dir with only notes.txt keep the old message;
  • --all still lists private symbols;
  • a file with one public and one private fn still shows the public one.
• Integration test: a new test in tests/integration.rs runs the real binary and pins the shell output.
• Positive control: switching the new branch off made the integration test fail by name; I restored it in the same command and it passed again.
• cargo fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, build and the full cargo test all pass, including module_size (commands_map.rs is now 1846 lines, under its 2000 cap).

Docs: the exit-code paragraph in docs/src/usage/commands.md quoted the empty message, so I added a sentence there describing the new "none public" case.
